    title_en: "Singapore Cyber Security Agency (CSA) Releases Consultation Conclusion Report: Revised Licensing Framework for Cybersecurity Service Providers",
    summary_en: "The Cyber Security Agency of Singapore (CSA) released a consultation conclusion report in April 2022 regarding the licensing framework for cybersecurity service providers under the Cybersecurity Act. This framework aims to enhance the security of cybersecurity services, improve industry standards, and address the information asymmetry between consumers and service providers. The report noted that while the industry generally supported the framework, some concerns were raised regarding potential stifling of innovation or excessive regulatory burden. In response to industry feedback, the CSA made revisions, such as: limiting the required information provision to only what is necessary for investigation purposes; requiring notification of key personnel changes within 14 days of the new key personnel's appointment; and restricting the scope of confidentiality obligations regarding client information, ensuring it does not impede professional activities such as threat intelligence collection using anonymized data or responsible vulnerability disclosure. These revisions aim to balance regulatory requirements with practical industry operational needs, providing clearer guidance for the sector.",
